Modifications to eve

The @open-everywhere/core package distributes patches/eve+0.71.0.patch. That
patch file is a modification of eve 0.71.0. Vercel licenses eve 0.71.0 under the
Apache License, Version 2.0. The copyright notice of eve 0.71.0 reads
"Copyright 2026 Vercel, Inc. and contributors". The Open Everywhere authors made
the changes in the patch file.

The patch modifies four files of eve 0.71.0:

  dist/src/execution/web-fetch/request.js
  dist/src/harness/tool-loop.js
  dist/src/internal/authored-package-boundary.js
  dist/src/protocol/message.d.ts

Open Everywhere does not ship the eve package. eve is a peer dependency, so the
consumer installs eve 0.71.0 from the registry. The patch file carries the
modified portions of eve. The oe-eve-patch command, which
@open-everywhere/core ships, applies them to the eve that the consumer
installed. The command patches no file outside the consumer's own project. To
restore an eve that holds an older Open Everywhere patch, it also writes to npm's
cache and to a temporary directory.

The attribution notice of eve 0.71.0 follows, as section 4(d) of the Apache
License, Version 2.0 requires. The notices for eve's bundled code-mode runtime
are not reproduced, because the patch modifies no part of that runtime.

